{% decision_card number="ADR-0002" status="approved" %}
One decision. Status reviewed 2026-07-27.
{% /decision_card %}

## Context

Beacon must earn local trust without loud agency claims or an impersonal software aesthetic.

## Decision drivers

- Plain-language trust
- One clear next action
- Accessibility
- Real local proof
- Consistent brand

## Options considered

- Generic software theme
- High-stimulation agency design
- Restrained editorial Beacon system

## Decision

Use the forest, sage, gold, cream, ink, and rule palette; Playfair and DM Sans hierarchy; one primary CTA; real photography; visible focus; reduced motion; and honest status language.

## Positive consequences

- Consistent experience
- Clear review rules
- Accessibility is a requirement

## Negative consequences

- Harder prioritization
- Real photography requires coordination

## Risks

- Decorative additions can dilute CTA hierarchy
- Color contrast can drift

## Follow-up work

- Review desktop/mobile/keyboard/reduced motion
- Use canonical CSS tokens

## Supersedes or superseded by

Consolidates earlier UI and brand choices; superseded by: none.

